body:
Our coaching is built on a polyvagal-informed model of the nervous system that we teach as the Nervous System Triangle. The nervous system governs three things:

1. whether the body is in survival mode or rest-and-digest mode;
2. automatic body functions such as heart rate, blood pressure, and breathing;
3. the immune system.

In a healthy person, the nervous system spends most of its time in rest-and-digest and switches into survival mode only when necessary. In CFS, Long COVID, and fibromyalgia this is flipped: survival mode becomes the default, and rest-and-digest becomes rare.
